"""
St Peter's Basilica, Vatican City (Q12512) — the basilica and St Peter's Square, built by code.

Author: Álvaro C. Chulvi (with AI assistance). Licence of the resulting model: CC BY 4.0.
The building: Donato Bramante (from 1506, died 1514), Raphael, Antonio da Sangallo the Younger, Michelangelo
(1546–1564: the apses, the giant order and the dome, died 1564), Giacomo della Porta (raised the dome 1588–1590,
died 1602), Carlo Maderno (nave and façade 1607–1614, died 1629); the square and its colonnade by Gian Lorenzo
Bernini (1656–1667, died 1680). Public domain.

Measurements (see meta.json for the sources):
- Plan: OpenStreetMap way 244159210 (the basilica, wikidata Q12512) and its building:parts (the dome, its
  lantern and cross, the four minor domes, the façade columns), relation 10044166 (Piazza San Pietro), way
  135747106 (Piazza Retta), way 149958437 and relation 12043628 (the two arms of Bernini's colonnade), ways
  246418139 and 255907697 (Braccio di Carlo Magno and Braccio di Costantino), the 305 colonnade columns mapped
  one by one (ways 2440450xx/2440952xx…), ways 244928138 and 244928574 (the fountains of Maderno and Bernini),
  way 799694267 (the obelisk), the eight paving sectors (relations 15843460–15843469). All in the axes of
  heading 89.2 with the origin on the cross of the dome (way 243927787).
- Heading: the axis of the basilica through the cross of the dome and the middle of the eight façade columns
  (OSM) runs at 89.2° (the façade outline is perpendicular to 89.35–89.45°). The obelisk, from OSM, falls 3.7 m
  north of that axis (Wikipedia it says 1.56 m), so the square is placed exactly where OSM has it.
- The basilica is drawn symmetric about its axis: the north half of the OSM outline (the south one has the
  bridges to the Sacristy), the apses as arcs fitted to OSM (transept apses r 18.6 m centred 59.7 m from the
  crossing, west apse r 18.4 m), length 217 m (Wikipedia it: 218 m), the façade 114.7 m wide (Wikipedia it:
  114.69 m; OSM: 115 m, 2.6 m off the axis — centred here). The OSM outline and its dome part lie 1–2.6 m
  south of the axis given by the mapped façade columns and the cross; the model follows the columns and the
  cross (within the ±2 m of the tracing).
- Heights (y = 0 = the floor of the basilica and of the portico): façade 45.44 m (Wikipedia it), with the
  giant Corinthian order to 29.0 m (columns ~27 m, estimated ±5 %), entablature to 34.0, attic to 43.6,
  cornice and balustrade to 45.44; the 13 statues (Christ, St John the Baptist, eleven apostles) 5.7 m
  (Wikipedia it: «over 5.7 m»); the clocks of Valadier (1785) on the end bays (size estimated). Michelangelo's
  body carries the same levels round the apses. Dome (Wikipedia it «Cupola di San Pietro»): top of the cross
  136.6 m (en: 136.6; it gives 133.3 m from the street and 136.57 in other sources), external diameter 49 m,
  58.9 m with the buttresses, 16 buttresses with paired columns, 16 ribs, lantern 17–18 m; OSM parts: base
  54–60 m, dome 60–110 m, lantern 110–134 m. Used here: platform 45.4–52.0, drum 52–70.5, attic to 77.6, shell
  to 109.8, lantern to 128.5, ball and cross to 136.6 (±3 % for the intermediate levels). Minor domes (OSM
  54–60 m, plan Ø 19–20 m): estimated, top of the cross 75.8 m (±10 %).
- Square: the obelisk shaft 25.5 m and 41 m to the top of the cross (Wikipedia en); the colonnade four columns
  deep (284 columns, 88 pilasters; 140 statues of saints), here the 305 OSM supports as Tuscan columns, 14 m to
  the top of the capitals and 16.9 m to the cornice (OSM 15/17 m), statues 3.2 m (estimated); the arms are
  circular arcs fitted to the OSM columns (north centre (34.6, 322.1), radii 66.4–84.9 m; south centre
  (−28.9, 323.2), radii 67.6–85.9 m). The ground: «the difference between the façade and the obelisk was
  reduced to 6 m» (Wikipedia it, about 3 %): the paving falls from y = 0 at the façade line to −3.0 at the
  foot of the steps (z = 225) and −6.0 at the obelisk, then −7.3 at the east end (from EU-DEM, ±1 m). The
  sagrato (from OSM) stands at 0 to −0.3 with 14 steps down to the square; the fountains (OSM Ø 10.3 m) and
  their mushroom bowls ~8 m high (estimated).
Colours: travertine for the basilica, the colonnade and the corridors, lead grey for the domes and the vault
roofs, dark grey sampietrini with travertine bands for the square.

Axes (docs/MODEL_SPEC.md): +Y up, the façade faces +Z (east, 89.2°), +X points north. Origin on the cross of the
dome; y = 0 at the floor of the basilica (the sagrato in front of the façade). "ground": "keep".

    python model_sources/Q12512_st_peters_basilica.py   -> models/Q12512/model.glb
"""
